{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1451010-arson-spirits","id":1451010,"title":"Arson Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-04T20:52:55-07:00","id":1451010,"title":"Arson Spirits","content":"The hanzerih-usum slither and slip their way into old buildings, nursing nests of embers among the kindling at their bases. They revel in destruction, delighting when small children discover the flickering power of BURNING for the first time. They slip into Twilight, lay fiery eggs wherever they go, which ignite when they return to the Shadow, where they can safely harvest the destructive resonance. Incendiary serpents look roughly like ordinary snakes at a glance, although most have too many eyes or multiple heads. Closer examination reveals that their scales are made of soot and ash, while orange sparks burn beneath their skin.<br /> <br /> Nuzusal frequently assume that the hanzerih-usum are in league with the Fire-Touched. Although the <i>Izdakh</i> go out of their way to patronize them, the arson spirits are more naturally drawn to Destroyer Wolf and the Blood Talons. To a lesser extent, the Bone Shadows and Predator Kings also curry their favour. Mages occasionally seek out the fire snakes as familiars, particularly revolutionarily-inclined Thyrsus, as well as Obrimos with a spiritual bent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Incendiary Serpent (Fire Snakes, Hanzerih-Usum) </b></span><br /> <i>Rank 1 Arson Spirit</i><br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 4 Finesse 3 Resistance 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 4<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>+4<br /> <b>Defense: </b>4<br /> <b>Speed: </b>10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>4<br /> <b>Influences: </b> Destruction \u2022<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast, Firestarter, Lay Embers*<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Twilight Form, Reaching<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must aid anyone who starts a bonfire for it.<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Fumes from a fire extinguisher<br /> <i>New Numen - Lay Embers (R):</i> By spending two Essence instead of one when activating Firestarter, the spirit delays the effect until the start of the next Scene.<br /> <br /> Incendiary serpents are too weak to Claim mortals on their own, but those with werewolf or mage allies still find ways to do so. Embers burn behind an Arson-Claimed\u2019s eyes and their face mutates, becoming like a charcoal serpent\u2019s. Their bodies are gaunt and wiry, their limbs move with uncanny grace, and fire burns within their veins.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Lay Claim (Wolf Rite \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This rite channels a werewolf\u2019s power into a Hursihim, allowing the least spirits to seize Flesh usually beyond their means. Predator Kings are particularly fond of using this rite to shove a hanzerih-usum into an unwitting mortal, then set them loose on a densely packed urban centre. More Uratha know this rite than are willing to admit to it, though, as Arson-Claimed are useful if unsubtle tools in the fight against the Pure.<br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Control, flesh, fire, nest<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 15 minutes)<br /> <b>Success: </b>This rite targets a human, who must be willing or restrained and must be performed at a Locus. At the climax of the ritual, the target becomes Open to all spirits who match the Locus\u2019 resonance for the remainder of the Scene. Any Rank 1 spirit the target is Open to can spend five Essence to Claim the target, even if they do not possess the Manifestation or have not placed the Controlled Condition on the target. The rite master has no control over the resulting Claimed, although werewolves frequently use the rite as a bargaining chip to extract promises from the spirit before performing the ritual.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Arson-Claimed</b></span><br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 2, Strength 4, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Craft 3 (Molotov Cocktails), Investigation 1 (Classified Documents), Politics 1, Science 2, Athletics 3 (Throwing), Firearms 2, Larceny 1, Stealth 3, Intimidation 2, Streetwise 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies (Hackers) 2, Anonymity 3, Area of Expertise (Molotov Cocktails)<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>4<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Initiative Modifier:</b> +7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Speed:</b>14<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Destruction \u2022<br /> <b>Dread Powers: </b>Fire Elemental, Swift<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must aid anyone who starts a bonfire for it.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Fumes from a fire extinguisher","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-04-2021, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T21:30:12-07:00","id":1451014,"title":"","content":"Influence over Destruction? Not Fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T21:56:20-07:00","id":1451019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1451010-arson-spirits?p=1451014#post1451014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influence over Destruction? Not Fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were Rank 2, they'd both be at one dot. But I see these spirits as being more at home in a junkyard or trash compactor than in a camp fire. They are ruinous little pricks who want to wreck and demolish everything around them. Fire's their preferred method, but if a werewolf wants to appease them by taking a sledgehammer to a building, they won't say no. So in my head, that says destruction spirit first, fire spirit second.<br /> <br /> Of course though, absolutely nothing breaks if you think fire works better and swap the influences around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T11:24:27-07:00","id":1451151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1451010-arson-spirits?p=1451019#post1451019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it were Rank 2, they'd both be at one dot. But I see these spirits as being more at home in a junkyard or trash compactor than in a camp fire. They are ruinous little pricks who want to wreck and demolish everything around them. Fire's their preferred method, but if a werewolf wants to appease them by taking a sledgehammer to a building, they won't say no. So in my head, that says destruction spirit first, fire spirit second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm pretty sure they wouldn't be the first elementals whose Influence was on something other than the direct material they're born from.<br /> <br /> Like, that can go with other spirits too. The Mage book Summoners features a briefcase spirit whose Influence is Protection.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T12:06:16-07:00","id":1451157,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting is that having Destruction as an influence is one of the reasons they are drawn to Destroyer Wolf's court. And that is an intentional choice, I wanted them associated with Blood Talons. Lay Claim effectively requires a human sacrifice, it is a profoundly evil thing to use. Easy enough to associate it with the Pure... but it's probably the Blood Talons who use it the most, which in mind is much more interesting/horrifying. Even if the PCs don't use it, it's a very quick way to create conflict between the Talons and the Storm Lords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T08:58:41-07:00","id":1451673,"title":"","content":"Ever seen cobwebs made from ash after a fire? These soot tags aren\u2019t actual webs, but magnetized particles congregating together following a blaze. Spiders never live inside them - at least in the Flesh. In the Shadow, massive black webs lurk in the corners of abandoned warehouses and dilapidated ruins. In these dark places lurk<i> hargishar-ushumfin</i>.<br /> <br /> Desolation Crawlers appear to be spiders the size of large dogs. Instead of an exoskeleton, it has cracked coal and burnt wood. Flames leap out from between its joints and its many fractal eyes burn like orange jewels. The Spiders Fetter themselves to the buildings they will destroy, abandoning them only after reducing them to cinders. A sure sign of a <i>hargishar-ushumfin</i> infestation is the dark webs they weave in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Despite their shared arachnid form, Burning Spiders harbour a deep hatred for the Azlu. The <i>hargishar-ushumfin </i>prefer it when the Gauntlet remains weak, allowing them to slip back and forth between Twilight and the Shadow. Canny werewolves use this to their advantage, making common cause with the Desolation Crawlers against their shared foes. Of course, the Spiders don\u2019t care for most packs either. They only show grudging respect for the Hunters In Darkness, Blood Talons, and Fire-Touched. For the latter two it is more out of deference for their Tribal Totems than any genuine appreciation.<br /> <br /> While Beasts don\u2019t always haunt the Shadow, the Begotten also show an affinity for the Desolation Crawlers, especially Eshmaki, Namtaru, and Talassii. For their part, the spirits don\u2019t understand why Beasts care about them, only half-listening when they start rambling about the Dark Mother. The Spiders do appreciate that Beasts are content to let them hunt in their own way, unlike the Forsaken and Pure.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Burning Spiders </b>(Desolation Crawlers, <i>hargishar-ushumfin</i>)</span><br /> <br /> Rank 3 Arson Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 4 Finesse 9 Resistance 7<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>10<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <br /> <b>Initiative:</b> +16<br /> <br /> <b>Defense: </b>4<br /> <br /> <b>Speed: </b>17<br /> <br /> <b>Size: </b>4<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus: </b>11<br /> <br /> <b>Influences: </b> Destruction \u2022, Fire \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast, Firestarter, Implant Mission, Left-Handed Spanner, Speed<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Fetter, Twilight Form, Reaching, Unfetter<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot damage a burnt building until the damage has been repaired.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> A wind that has never carried smoke or ash","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T14:25:52-07:00","id":1453718,"title":"","content":"There's an episode of Castle prominently featuring an act of arson that makes me think something interesting might be made of spirits related to motives to do it. Both the financial and the emotional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}